    "from_name": "Casey Example",
    "re_line": "Re: Dispute of Overcharge on Account FB-2026-000002",
    "body": "Dear Billing Office,\n\nI am writing to dispute a charge on my account FB-2026-000002, dated 2026-08-12. I was billed $449.00 for code 71046 (Chest X-ray, 2 views) on line 5, but your published price file shows the cash price for this service should be $269.40, not $449.00.\n\nAccording to your own price file row 14756, code 71046 Chest Pa & Lat(Routine)2 Views has a discounted cash price of $269.40. I am a self-pay patient and should receive this price. The difference between what I was charged and what your price file lists is $179.60.\n\nUnder 45 CFR 180.50, I have the right to the prices your hospital publishes. I am asking you to correct this overcharge and adjust my bill to reflect the $269.40 cash price for code 71046.\n\nPlease respond by 2026-09-14 with a corrected bill or explanation. I also ask that you pause any collection activity on this account while this dispute is being reviewed.\n\nSincerely,\nCasey Example\n\nSources:\n- The hospital's own standard-charges file, row 14756: 71046 Chest Pa & Lat(Routine)2 Views, posted gross $449.00, discounted cash price $269.40 (file fetched 2026-09-13). https://www.normanregional.com/documents/PFS/736048282_norman-regional-health-system_standardcharges.csv\n- 45 CFR 180.50 requires this hospital to publish its standard charges, including the discounted cash price, in a machine-readable file. https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-45/part-180",
    "citations": [
